    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9775" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conceptācŭlum</span></b> ,
		i, n.
		concipio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that which receives something, a receptacle</i>
			(post-Aug. and rare). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Prop., <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 45, 44, § 115</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sanguinis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 18, 10, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Front. Aquaed. 22
			al.</span></i>—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">superbia aliubi conceptaculum, sed hic (sc. in
					superciliis) sedem habet,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 51, § 138</span></i>
			.</div>
